Optionally drop the CJK encodings from mbstring to shrink the image.

The bundled libmbfl carries the legacy CJK (Chinese/Japanese/Korean) codec tables in
mbfilter_cjk.c -- ~740 KB of the ~965 KB mbstring costs. When built with
-DPHP_EXT_MBSTRING_NO_CJK, mbfilter_cjk.c and mbfilter_utf8_mobile.c (which reuses the
CJK emoji tables) are left out of the build; this patch then drops, behind the
MBSTRING_NO_CJK macro, everything that would otherwise reference the missing symbols:
the CJK/mobile entries in the encoding registry, the sjis_mac fast-path check in
mb_substr, and the mb_convert_kana() function (Japanese kana, backed by a table in
mbfilter_cjk.c). UTF-8/UTF-16/Latin and everything else keep working. Without the macro
this is a no-op (all encodings and mb_convert_kana present).

